cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Reproducibility package for "Quantifying transient biochemical information in
  Escherichia coli chemotaxis"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (via its Zenodo DOI)
  and the associated article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: De la Fuente
    given-names: Ildefonso M.
  - family-names: Carrasco-Pujante
    given-names: José
  - family-names: Fedetz
    given-names: María
  - family-names: Legarreta
    given-names: Leire
  - family-names: Malaina
    given-names: Iker
  - family-names: Pérez-Yarza
    given-names: Gorka
  - family-names: Martínez
    given-names: Luis
  - family-names: Cortés
    given-names: Jesús M.
  - family-names: López
    given-names: José I.
license: MIT
repository-code: 'https://github.com/JoseCarrascoPujante/ecoli-chemotaxis-information'
abstract: >-
  Standalone Python script and executable Jupyter notebook reproducing the
  principal recalculable quantitative results of the manuscript: microscopic and
  collective methylation capacity, endpoint-based recalibration of the Shimizu et
  al. (2010) fixed-modification FRET data, bootstrap and structural sensitivity
  analyses, FRET-to-methylation noise mapping, static mutual information and
  information-equivalent distinguishability, environmental-prior sensitivity,
  run-scale and timescale calculations, the kinase-information benchmark, and
  boundary-treatment ratios.
keywords:
  - Escherichia coli
  - chemotaxis
  - receptor methylation
  - information theory
  - mutual information
  - reproducibility
